# bytes (D102, D115): their own type, read and written explicitly.
greeting is bytes from text "Grüße"
say greeting
say length of greeting
say hex from bytes greeting
say base64 from bytes greeting
say text from bytes greeting
fromHex is bytes from hex " 4772c3bcc39f65 "
if fromHex is greeting
    say "hex and text agree"
.
fromBase64 is bytes from base64 "R3LDvMOfZQ=="
if fromBase64 is greeting
    say "base64 agrees"
.
nothing is empty bytes
say nothing length of nothing
if nothing
    say "empty bytes are still true"
.
if greeting is "Grüße"
    say "wrong"
otherwise
    say "bytes never equal text"
.
mixed are
    "a"
.
add greeting to mixed
say mixed
write bytes greeting to file "out/data.bin"
copied is bytes from file "out/data.bin"
say text from bytes copied
write bytes copied to file "out/data.bin" atomically
read "out/data.bin" into asText
say asText
bytes is 5
hex is "not special here"
text is "neither"
say bytes hex text
bad are
    "4772C3BC C39F65"
    "48656C6C6"
    "zz"
    ""
.
for each source in bad
    try
        x is bytes from hex source
    otherwise into reason
        say reason
    .
.
try
    x is bytes from base64 "!!!"
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    x is text from bytes "plain"
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    x is text from bytes bytes from hex "FF"
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    write bytes "text" to file "x.bin"
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    x is bytes from file "missing.bin"
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    total is greeting plus 1
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    convert greeting to json into json
    say json
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
